  "description": "Factor IX variants secreted from human cells and tethered to their surface (MultiSTEP), stained at their C-terminal strep II tag and sorted into four bins of signal. The 461-residue protein in three overlapping tiles (positions 146–164 and 299–318 are in two), each in three biological replicates. The authors scored each replicate by the weighted average of the bins (0.25–1), set the median of the wild type's barcodes to 1 and the lowest 5% of missense variants to 0, and averaged the replicates.",
